add(2007,3,4,'A logarithmic potential gives a lower bound by following the larger piece at each cut; parallel bisections attain it.','Parallel stages for cutting a rectangular grid',r'An $m\times n$ grid must be cut into unit squares. In each stage, any collection of current rectangular pieces may each be cut once along a grid line. What is the minimum number of stages?',r'The minimum is $\lceil\log_2m\rceil+\lceil\log_2n\rceil$. A cut in an $a\times b$ rectangle leaves one child whose cut dimension is at least half the previous one. Therefore the quantity $\lceil\log_2a\rceil+\lceil\log_2b\rceil$ decreases by at most 1 along a suitable chain of descendants. A unit square has value 0, proving the lower bound. For attainment, bisect the row dimension as evenly as possible in every current piece at each stage, until all heights are 1; this takes $\lceil\log_2m\rceil$ stages. Repeat in the column dimension for $\lceil\log_2n\rceil$ stages.','Combinatorics',['Algorithms','Extremal bounds','Binary splitting','Monovariants'],source=s)
add(2007,4,2.5,'Pair symmetric powers; each pair is at most 1+r^(2n+1), and r=1 proves sharpness.',source=s)
add(2007,5,4,'Multiplying and dividing line products forces the common product to be the central entry cubed; a nontrivial distinct-entry construction attains the sole cube in range.','A multiplicative magic square',r'A $3\times3$ array of distinct positive integers has the same product $P$ in each row, column and diagonal. Show that exactly one $P$ lies between 5000 and 6500, and construct an array attaining it.',r'Write the entries rowwise as $a,b,c;d,e,f;g,h,i$. Multiplying the two diagonal products and the middle-row product and dividing by the first and third column products gives $e^3=P$. The only cube in the specified interval is $18^3=5832$. It is attained by the rows $(2,81,36)$, $(324,18,1)$, $(9,4,162)$. All nine numbers are distinct, and direct multiplication verifies that every row, column and diagonal has product 5832.','Algebra',['Algebraic identities','Integer constraints','Constructions'],source=s)
